Verse 1:
[C/G]Lord, [Em]I [G7/F]have made [C/E]Thy [G]word [F]my choice,
[G]My [C/E]lasting [Em]heritage;
[G]There shall my [C]noblest [Dm/A]powers rejoice,
[Am]My warmest thoughts [G7/F]engage.

Verse 2:
[C/G]I'll [Em]read [G7/F]the histories [F]of Thy [Em]love,
[G]And [C/E]keep [G]Thy [Em]laws in [Am]sight;
[G]While through [C]Thy promises [Dm/A]I rove,
[Am]With ever fresh [G7/F]delight.

Verse 3:
[C/G]In [Em]this [G7/F]broad land [C/E]of [G]wealth [F]unknown,
[G]Where [C/E]springs [G]of [Em]life arise,
[G]Seeds of immortal [Dm/A]bliss are sown,
[Am]And hidden glory [C/E]lies.

Verse 4:
[C/G]The [Em]best [G7/F]relief [C/E]that [G]mourners [F]have,
[G]It [C/E]makes [Em]our sorrows [Am]blest;
[G]Our fairest [C]hope [Dm/A]beyond [Am]the [Dm]grave,
[Am]And our [Dm/A]eternal [C/E]rest.
